**Claimed critical; verifier found:** verifier off

Any authenticated caller can pass `accountId` in the JSON body and read another account. The comment mentions support staff, but there is no role or permission check before using the client-supplied id — only `auth(req)` ran, which previously bound the lookup to `caller.accountId`.

**Failure mode:** user A sends `{"accountId":"<victim>"}` and receives the victim account record via `Response.json(account)`.

**Fix:** only honor `body.accountId` when the caller is authorized staff (e.g. `caller.isStaff` / equivalent); otherwise always use `caller.accountId`. Prefer a separate staff-only route if that matches your access model.

```suggestion
  const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
  const id: string = (caller.isStaff && body.accountId) ? body.accountId : caller.accountId;
  const account = await db.accounts.findUnique({ where: { id } });
```

(Adapt `caller.isStaff` to whatever staff claim your `auth` helper actually exposes.)
